  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1986-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(2 \\lt \\sqrt{8} \\lt 3\\) and \\(8 \\lt \\sqrt{80} \\lt 9,\\) the whole numbers strictly between \\(\\sqrt{8}\\) and \\(\\sqrt{80}\\) are \\(3,\\) \\(4,\\) \\(5,\\) \\(6,\\) \\(7,\\) \\(8.\\) There are six of them.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Find perfect squares just above \\(8\\) and just below \\(80\\)",
        "\\(\\sqrt{8}\\) is between \\(2\\) and \\(3,\\) and \\(\\sqrt{80}\\) is between \\(8\\) and \\(9\\)"
      ],
